            <ArticleTitle>The White Paper on opioids and pain: a pan-European challenge: the European White Paper on the use of opioids in chronic pain management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-87</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This document was developed by a group of over two dozen pain clinicians and investigators from Austria, Belgium, Denmark, France, Germany Ireland, Israel, Italy, The Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Portugal. Spain, Sweden, Switzerland and the United Kingdom and funded by an educational grant form Mundipharma International, Limited. The stated aim of the White Paper is to identify inequalities in government policies towards opioids that contribute to inadequate treatment of pain. It calls for their replacement with policies that will support doctors and patients in their efforts to relieve pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
